window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/resources/hpc-v27-028-79e18cec03919847.json"]={sha256:"79e18cec03919847967859c23ed4c3e81d4183b59dfea27caba426a7f3cc1db4",value:{"sources":[{"id":"v27-case-09b7a0c58148145b","url":"https://docs.kernel.org/networking/bonding.html","title":"Linux Ethernet Bonding Driver HOWTO","titleEn":"Linux Ethernet Bonding Driver HOWTO","publisher":"Linux kernel project","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."}],"media":{"courses":[{"courseId":"hpc-v27-028","videos":[],"guides":[]}]},"related":{"courses":[{"courseId":"hpc-v27-028","related":[{"id":"hpc-v27-029","referenceUrls":["https://docs.kernel.org/networking/timestamping.html"],"title":"PTP 時戳：單向延遲的時鐘不確定界","titleEn":"PTP timestamps: clock uncertainty in one-way latency","why":"用兩課的可觀察驗收條件比較模型邊界：交付故障分類、四階段時間線、封包暴露表與載波盲點反例；不操作實際網路介面；請同學只使用交付件重算兩組，保留失敗案例與限制；全程使用合成檔案，不對生產系統執行故障。","whyEn":"Compare model boundaries using observable acceptance criteria: Deliver failure classes, the four-stage timeline, packet-exposure table and a carrier-monitor blind-spot example. The exercise never disables or reconfigures the learner’s actual network interfaces. Have a peer reproduce both configurations from the artifacts, retaining failed cases and limitations. Use synthetic files throughout; never inject these faults into a production system.","difference":"記錄 send_clock、receive_clock、時戳來源層級、offset_bound 與校時時間；拒絕混用軟體與硬體時間戳而不註記。","differenceEn":"Record sending and receiving clock identities, timestamping layer, offset bound and synchronization age. Mark mixed software and hardware timestamps explicitly instead of treating them as interchangeable observations.","transfer":"保留單位與邊界條件，僅轉移可證明相容的驗證方法。","transferEn":"Retain units and boundary conditions; transfer only demonstrably compatible verification methods.","practice":["固定供給且完全黑洞的模型中，暴露封包量為封包率乘偵測延遲；此量不等於最終不可恢復的應用資料；供給率每秒 2000 包；偵測延遲名義 0.3 秒、變更 0.05 秒；切換後立即恢復是教學假設；名義式 2000*0.3 = 600 packets exposed；變更式 2000*0.05 = 100 packets exposed。所有數值、限制與門檻為原創合成教學條件；來源支援概念與介面，不代表實機量測或設備規格。","若觀察差值 d、兩時鐘差的絕對誤差界 e，真實延遲位於 [d-e,d+e]；負下界表示無法辨識正延遲而非真的逆時；觀察單向差值 10 微秒；相對時鐘誤差界由 2 增為 8 微秒；數值檢查計算下界；名義式 10-2 = 8 microseconds lower bound；變更式 10-8 = 2 microseconds lower bound。所有數值、限制與門檻為原創合成教學條件；來源支援概念與介面，不代表實機量測或設備規格。","比較兩個模型的輸入、誤差與驗收條件，記錄不能沿用的假設。"],"practiceEn":["Under constant offered rate and a complete blackhole, exposed packets equal packet rate times detection delay. This is not necessarily permanently lost application data because retries and transport recovery are separate. Offer 2000 packets per second. Detection delay changes from 0.3 to 0.05 seconds, with immediate recovery after detection assumed for the fixture rather than asserted for real bonding behavior. Nominal 2000*0.3 = 600 packets exposed; changed 2000*0.05 = 100 packets exposed. Every numeric input, limit and threshold is an original synthetic teaching condition. References establish concepts and interfaces, not measured machine results or equipment specifications.","For observed difference d and a bound e on relative clock error, true latency lies between d-e and d+e. A negative lower bound signals insufficient timing certainty, not backward packet travel. Observe a 10-microsecond timestamp difference. Relative clock uncertainty changes from 2 to 8 microseconds; the numeric checks calculate the lower endpoint, with upper endpoints retained in the evidence table. Nominal 10-2 = 8 microseconds lower bound; changed 10-8 = 2 microseconds lower bound. Every numeric input, limit and threshold is an original synthetic teaching condition. References establish concepts and interfaces, not measured machine results or equipment specifications.","Compare inputs, errors, and criteria; document assumptions that cannot be transferred."]},{"id":"hpc-v27-038","referenceUrls":["https://openzfs.github.io/openzfs-docs/Basic%20Concepts/Operations/Scrub%20and%20Resilver.html"],"title":"OpenZFS scrub：校驗發現與可修復副本矩陣","titleEn":"OpenZFS scrub: detecting corruption and identifying repairable copies","why":"用兩課的可觀察驗收條件比較模型邊界：交付故障分類、四階段時間線、封包暴露表與載波盲點反例；不操作實際網路介面；請同學只使用交付件重算兩組，保留失敗案例與限制；全程使用合成檔案，不對生產系統執行故障。","whyEn":"Compare model boundaries using observable acceptance criteria: Deliver failure classes, the four-stage timeline, packet-exposure table and a carrier-monitor blind-spot example. The exercise never disables or reconfigures the learner’s actual network interfaces. Have a peer reproduce both configurations from the artifacts, retaining failed cases and limitations. Use synthetic files throughout; never inject these faults into a production system.","difference":"每列為 block_id、expected_digest、copyA、copyB、backup_digest；先判斷每份是否可信，再判斷邏輯區塊。","differenceEn":"Record block identity, expected digest, both copies and any backup digest. Validate individual copies first, then classify logical blocks as healthy, repairable or unrecoverable.","transfer":"保留單位與邊界條件，僅轉移可證明相容的驗證方法。","transferEn":"Retain units and boundary conditions; transfer only demonstrably compatible verification methods.","practice":["固定供給且完全黑洞的模型中，暴露封包量為封包率乘偵測延遲；此量不等於最終不可恢復的應用資料；供給率每秒 2000 包；偵測延遲名義 0.3 秒、變更 0.05 秒；切換後立即恢復是教學假設；名義式 2000*0.3 = 600 packets exposed；變更式 2000*0.05 = 100 packets exposed。所有數值、限制與門檻為原創合成教學條件；來源支援概念與介面，不代表實機量測或設備規格。","教學雙副本模型中，至少有一份通過預期 checksum 的區塊才可恢復；可恢復比例為合格區塊數除總數；一百個邏輯區塊，其中三個只有一份壞、兩個兩份皆壞，其餘正常；變更用已驗證備份修復那兩個區塊；名義式 (100-2)/100*100 = 98 % recoverable blocks；變更式 100/100*100 = 100 % recoverable blocks。所有數值、限制與門檻為原創合成教學條件；來源支援概念與介面，不代表實機量測或設備規格。","比較兩個模型的輸入、誤差與驗收條件，記錄不能沿用的假設。"],"practiceEn":["Under constant offered rate and a complete blackhole, exposed packets equal packet rate times detection delay. This is not necessarily permanently lost application data because retries and transport recovery are separate. Offer 2000 packets per second. Detection delay changes from 0.3 to 0.05 seconds, with immediate recovery after detection assumed for the fixture rather than asserted for real bonding behavior. Nominal 2000*0.3 = 600 packets exposed; changed 2000*0.05 = 100 packets exposed. Every numeric input, limit and threshold is an original synthetic teaching condition. References establish concepts and interfaces, not measured machine results or equipment specifications.","In the two-copy fixture, a block is recoverable only if at least one copy matches its expected checksum. Recoverable fraction divides qualifying logical blocks by total blocks, not good replicas by replica count. Use one hundred logical blocks: three have one bad copy, two have both copies bad and the rest are healthy. Restore the two unrecoverable blocks from a separately verified backup in the changed fixture. Nominal (100-2)/100*100 = 98 % recoverable blocks; changed 100/100*100 = 100 % recoverable blocks. Every numeric input, limit and threshold is an original synthetic teaching condition. References establish concepts and interfaces, not measured machine results or equipment specifications.","Compare inputs, errors, and criteria; document assumptions that cannot be transferred."]}],"references":[{"id":"v27-case-931f803098f1b483","url":"https://docs.kernel.org/networking/timestamping.html","title":"Timestamping","titleEn":"Timestamping","publisher":"Linux kernel project","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."},{"id":"v27-case-9406619b083fe9e7","url":"https://openzfs.github.io/openzfs-docs/Basic%20Concepts/Operations/Scrub%20and%20Resilver.html","title":"Scrub and Resilver","titleEn":"Scrub and Resilver","publisher":"OpenZFS project","scope":"查證具名案例與原理背景。課內數值、故障資料與判準為原創教學假設；請勿當作廠商規格或操作程序。","scopeEn":"Establish named case and principle context. Numbers, fault data, and criteria are original teaching assumptions, not manufacturer specifications or operating procedures."}],"overview":"比較相鄰案例與另一組案例的模型、可量測結果及可轉移的驗證方法。","overviewEn":"Compare neighboring and cross-group cases by model, measurable outcome, and transferable verification method."}]},"places":{"courses":[]},"vendors":{"courses":[],"vendors":[]}}};
